<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <h1>Meet Our Tampa Bay Fishing Guides</h1>
  <p class="lead">Four captains, each running his own boat and his own business, who book together under one name. Between them: 95+ years on this water and 133 five star Google reviews.</p>
</div></section>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="cap-row" id="ashmore">
    <img src="/images/capt-ashmore.webp" alt="Capt. William Ashmore holding a redfish" width="640" height="411">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. William Ashmore</h2>
      <p class="tag">Gatorbacks Fishing Charters · Florida native · 40+ years · USCG 100 GRT Master</p>
      <p>Capt. Ashmore grew up in Florida and has fished Tampa Bay and Central Florida for more than 40 years. He holds a USCG Master license for vessels up to 100 gross tons.</p>
      <p>He runs our <a href="/offshore-fishing/">offshore trips</a> past the nine mile line, and he is one of two captains on the <a href="/crappie-fishing/">crappie lakes</a> near Kissimmee. He also fishes <a href="/inshore/">inshore</a> and <a href="/nearshore/">nearshore</a>.</p>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"Captain Ashmore did a fantastic job of putting us on the fish all day long! He was so very accommodating and personable. He kept everyone engaged with his knowledge of Tampa Bay and its ecosystem."</p><footer>Randy P., Google review</footer></blockquote>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"Lots of knowledge with a calm cool demeanor. Caught fish all day every spot we stopped at!"</p><footer>Guest review, Gatorbacks Fishing Charters</footer></blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row" id="pruner">
    <img src="/images/capt-pruner.webp" alt="Capt. David Pruner on the boat" width="1240" height="1023">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. David Pruner</h2>
      <p class="tag">Hooked On Tampa Bay Fishing Charters · 25 years · Ruskin</p>
      <p>In his own words: "My journey with the rod and reel started 25 years ago, but the seeds were sown much earlier in the quiet lakes of Indiana with my Dad."</p>
      <p>"He was the one who taught me that patience and persistence aren't just virtues, they're the secret ingredients to reeling in success, both in life and fishing!"</p>
      <p>Capt. Pruner fishes from Bradenton Beach up into Tampa Bay out of Ruskin, on a 23 foot Sea Pro bay boat with a 200 horsepower Suzuki. The boat was built in 2004 and restored in 2018. His water is <a href="/inshore/">inshore</a> and <a href="/nearshore/">nearshore</a>: <a href="/redfish/">redfish</a>, <a href="/snook/">snook</a>, trout and the bottom fish just past the beaches.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row" id="gonzalez">
    <img src="/images/capt-gonzales.webp" alt="Capt. Frankie Gonzalez holding a snook" width="619" height="826" style="object-position:top">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. Frankie Gonzalez</h2>
      <p class="tag">FG Charters · Born and raised here · 30 years inshore</p>
      <p>Capt. Gonzalez has fished from Tampa Bay north into the Nature Coast for 30 years, and guests hear quickly that he grew up on this water. He runs a 2014 Pathfinder, 22 feet, with a 250 horsepower Yamaha.</p>
      <p>He takes <a href="/inshore/">inshore</a>, <a href="/nearshore/">nearshore</a>, <a href="/shark/">shark</a>, <a href="/tarpon/">tarpon</a> and <a href="/crappie-fishing/">crappie</a> trips. Many of his reviews come from parents who brought their kids.</p>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"He took me and my two nephews out fishing, and we had an absolute blast. ... We ended up catching over 80 fish! It was non-stop action, and the boys haven't stopped talking about it since."</p><footer>Kyle N., Google review, April 2025</footer></blockquote>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"You can tell Frankie knows the bay like the back of his hand, as he shared with us that he was born and raised in the area."</p><footer>Kim H., Google review, May 2025</footer></blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row" id="hahn">
    <img src="/images/capt-hahn.webp" alt="Capt. Rob Hahn holding a gag grouper" width="1102" height="1400" style="object-position:center 18%">
    <div>
      <h2>Capt. Rob Hahn</h2>
      <p class="tag">Barotrauma Fishing Charters · Certified Master Diver · Offshore</p>
      <p>Capt. Hahn is a certified Master Diver who has spent years underwater on the same wrecks, reefs and ledges he now fishes. He knows how the fish use that structure because he has been down there with them.</p>
      <p>He fishes a 25 foot Sailfish center console, dropping baits 40 to 100 feet or more for <a href="/grouper/">grouper</a> and snapper. His business is named for barotrauma, the pressure injury reef fish suffer when pulled up from depth, and he carries the descending device Florida requires to send released fish back down.</p>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"Captain took us to all his best spots and it was fish on every stop we did !!"</p><footer>Davi C., Google review</footer></blockquote>
      <blockquote class="cap-quote"><p>"He knew right where to take us so we could catch plenty of fish!!!"</p><footer>Chelsey H., Google review, March 2026</footer></blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap-row cap-reviews">
    <div>
      <h2>Where our reviews come from</h2>
      <p>Each captain collects reviews on his own business's Google profile, and a few come to Charter Fishing Tampa Bay directly. As of November 2026: Gatorbacks Fishing Charters 68, FG Charters 37, Charter Fishing Tampa Bay 12, Barotrauma Fishing Charters 10 and Hooked On Tampa Bay 6, all five stars.</p>
      <p>Read a selection on our <a href="/reviews/">reviews page</a>, browse the <a href="/gallery/">photo gallery</a>, or see what each trip is like on the <a href="/charters/">charters page</a>. Questions about licenses, kids or weather are answered in our <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>, and you can <a href="/contact-us/">message us</a> to match your group with a captain.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
